{{Quote|HELD trigger weapons create a continuous beam and have a short warm up time to reach full Damage|In-Game Description}}
'''Continuous Weapons''' (also known as '''Beam Weapons''') have attacks that fire a continuous beam or stream between the weapon and its target in a fully automatic fashion.

==Characteristics==
Continuous weapons share these common features:
*[[Trigger Type]] is listed as "Held".
*Relatively high [[fire rate]].
*Pinpoint [[accuracy]].
**Barely affected by {{M|Heavy Caliber}}'s and {{M|Magnum Force}}'s accuracy penalty.
*No [[recoil]].
*[[Hitscan]]. Damage ticks are instantaneous upon holding trigger.
*Consumes 0.5 ammo per tick of damage (although not true for some continuous weapons).
**Each tick is equal to 1/MODDED_FIRE_RATE.
*Initial damage starts at a lower percentage, and ramps up to 100% of its damage over 0.6 seconds of hitting a target. 0.8 seconds after the weapon stops hitting a target, the damage decays back to its initial point over 2 seconds.
**For most weapons, this lower percentage is 20%.
*Multiple hits on the same target from [[Multishot]] are combined, producing a damage instance with damage and [[Status Chance]] equal to the sum of all hits.
**This results in the same average number of status effects but causes damaging status effects to deal far more damage, since each status effect is based on the total damage of the weapon rather than one multishot instance.
**More information on [[Multishot#Continuous Weapons|Multishot]] respective subsection.
*Limited [[range]] that can be increased with {{M|Sinister Reach}} and {{M|Ruinous Extension}}.

==Unique Mechanics==
{{Community}}
Some continuous weapons offer unique mechanics not seen in any other weapon class.
*"Beam chaining" - initial beam can attack secondary targets from the primary target
**E.g. {{Weapon|Amprex}}, {{Weapon|Atomos}}, {{Weapon|Basmu}}'s alt-fire, {{Weapon|Gaze (Secondary)}}, {{Weapon|Kuva Nukor}}, {{Weapon|Larkspur}} ({{Weapon|Larkspur Prime|Prime}}), {{Weapon|Tenet Cycron}}, {{Weapon|Tenet Glaxion}}, {{Resource|Torid Incarnon Genesis}}, {{Resource|Boar Incarnon Genesis}}, and {{Weapon|Vermisplicer (Primary)}}.
**Each subsequent chain beam deals less damage.
**Mods like {{M|Firestorm}} will increase the range at which a beam can link to another enemy.
**[[Punch Through]] will cause the beam to rapidly recalculate which enemies are chained to, spreading out on the damage, but not increasing it.
**The range of chain beams are not affected by [[Beam Length]] bonuses.
**Additional chain beams do not consume ammo.
*"Split beam" - more than one beam that converges into a single focal point when [[zoom]]ed
**E.g. {{Weapon|Convectrix}} and {{Weapon|Phage}}
*"Homing beam" - beam that automatically seeks targets near the reticle
**E.g. {{Weapon|Klebrik Scaffold}} and {{Weapon|Vermisplicer (Secondary)}}
*"Conal beam" - beam that spreads out like a cone, similar to a flamethrower
**E.g. {{Weapon|Embolist}}, {{Weapon|Ignis}} family, and {{Weapon|Lega Prism}}

